   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Joe Thanks for the prompt reply.<div><br></div><div>So the annual variable is actually a data.frame. Is it possible to pass a data.frame into the markdown file? </div><div><br></div><div>What I intend to do is basically in the shiny app, I want to get some inputs (text and select) and then run a bunch of functions based on those two inputs to get the data.frame and store that data.frame into a variable called annual. Then pass that annual variable into the markdown file and create the html file through the render function and save it into a folder called outputTest, Then display that html file within the shiny app as well. Ca you guide me through that?</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Thursday, March 10, 2016 at 11:23:25 PM UTC-5, Joe Cheng [RStudio] wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Variables like this must be passed in explicitly. See this feature: <a href=\"http://rmarkdown.rstudio.com/developer_parameterized_reports.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rmarkdown.rstudio.com/developer_parameterized_reports.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792394327216000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Dd8BXtoBSgJNWIZh64o7m\">http://rmarkdown.rstudio.com/developer_parameterized_reports.html</a><br><br>I don&#39;t think this belongs in a reactive though, maybe in a renderUI that calls render and then does includeHTML on the result?<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Thu, Mar 10, 2016 at 8:19 PM Cullan Liang &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">cul...@liangbros.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:17.7273px\">My render function to create the html file from the rmd file is as follows:</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:17.7273px\"><br></p><pre style=\"padding:5px;overflow:auto;width:auto;max-height:600px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#3